From: Wisp Contributors <wisp@wisp.dev>
Date: April 29, 2026
Subject: feat: add Wisp CLI agent detection to Warp

This patch adds Wisp as a recognized third-party CLI agent in Warp.
Wisp is an open-source, local-first coding agent powered by Ollama.

When users run `wisp` in Warp's terminal, the agent toolbelt will
activate — rich input editor, code review panel, vertical tab metadata,
session sharing, and all other third-party agent features.

Changes to: app/src/terminal/cli_agent.rs

---

diff --git a/app/src/terminal/cli_agent.rs b/app/src/terminal/cli_agent.rs
index abc123..def456 100644
--- a/app/src/terminal/cli_agent.rs
+++ b/app/src/terminal/cli_agent.rs
@@ -93,6 +93,12 @@ const AUGGIE_COLOR: ColorU = ColorU {
 const CURSOR_COLOR: ColorU = ColorU {
     r: 38, g: 37, b: 30, a: 255,
 };

+/// Wisp brand color — indigo/violet (#6366F1)
+const WISP_COLOR: ColorU = ColorU {
+    r: 99, g: 102, b: 241, a: 255,
+};
+
 /// Represents a CLI agent (e.g., Claude Code, Gemini CLI, Codex, Amp, Droid,
-/// OpenCode, Copilot, Pi, Auggie, Cursor)
+/// OpenCode, Copilot, Pi, Auggie, Cursor, or Wisp)
 #[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, Sequence, Serialize, Deserialize)]
 pub enum CLIAgent {
     Claude,
@@ -107,6 +113,7 @@ pub enum CLIAgent {
     Auggie,
     CursorCli,
+    Wisp,
     /// Represents an unknown/custom CLI agent matched by user-configured regex patterns.
     Unknown,
 }
@@ -123,6 +130,7 @@ impl CLIAgent {
             CLIAgent::Auggie => "auggie",
             CLIAgent::CursorCli => "agent",
+            CLIAgent::Wisp => "wisp",
             CLIAgent::Unknown => "",
         }
     }
@@ -144,6 +152,7 @@ impl CLIAgent {
             CLIAgent::Auggie => "Auggie",
             CLIAgent::CursorCli => "Cursor",
+            CLIAgent::Wisp => "Wisp",
             CLIAgent::Unknown => "CLI Agent",
         }
     }
@@ -162,6 +171,7 @@ impl CLIAgent {
             CLIAgent::Auggie => Some(Icon::AuggieLogo),
             CLIAgent::CursorCli => Some(Icon::CursorLogo),
+            CLIAgent::Wisp => Some(Icon::WispLogo),
             CLIAgent::Unknown => None,
         }
     }
@@ -179,6 +189,7 @@ impl CLIAgent {
             CLIAgent::Auggie => &[SkillProvider::Agents],
             CLIAgent::CursorCli => &[SkillProvider::Agents],
+            CLIAgent::Wisp => &[SkillProvider::Agents],
             CLIAgent::Unknown => &[],
         }
     }
@@ -222,6 +233,7 @@ impl CLIAgent {
             CLIAgent::Auggie => Some(AUGGIE_COLOR),
             CLIAgent::CursorCli => Some(CURSOR_COLOR),
+            CLIAgent::Wisp => Some(WISP_COLOR),
             CLIAgent::Unknown => None,
         }
     }
@@ -233,6 +245,7 @@ impl CLIAgent {
             CLIAgent::Auggie => ColorU::new(0, 0, 0, 255),
             CLIAgent::Droid => ColorU::new(0, 0, 0, 255),
+            CLIAgent::Wisp => ColorU::new(0, 0, 0, 255),
             _ => ColorU::white(),
         }
     }

---

## Additional Steps

After the code change:

1. **Add Wisp's SVG icon** to `crates/warp_core/resources/bundled/svg/wisp.svg`
2. **Register the icon** in `crates/warp_core/src/ui/icons.rs`:
   ```rust
   Icon::WispLogo => "bundled/svg/wisp.svg",
   ```

### Test Plan

1. Build Warp from source
2. Run `wisp "explain the project structure"` in Warp's terminal
3. Verify the agent toolbelt appears with "Wisp" label
4. Verify rich input editor (`Ctrl+G`) works
5. Verify code review panel works
6. Verify vertical tab shows "Wisp" metadata
